RAMANUJAN SERIES
→ 515.9 → Analysis / Infinite Series

```
RAMANUJAN  1 + 2 + 3 + 4 + ...  =  -1/12

SERIES
  s  =  sum_{n=1 to inf} n
  Type: divergent (harmonic-like, linear growth)
  Partial sums:
    s_N = N(N+1)/2   -->  +infinity   as N --> inf
  Ordinary sum does not exist.

REGULARIZED VALUE
  Ramanujan summation assigns   s  =  -1/12
  Riemann zeta analytic continuation:
    zeta(s) = sum n^{-s}     (Re s > 1)
    zeta(-1) = -1/12
  Type: regularization (not Cauchy / ordinary summation)
  The number is real; the method extracts a finite part
  from an otherwise infinite expression.

KEY DISTINCTION
  Ordinary addition   : partial sums grow without bound
  Regularization      : assigns a consistent finite value
                        used in analysis and physics
                        (Casimir effect, bosonic strings)

RAMANUJAN
  Srinivasa Ramanujan
  Born 22 Dec 1887  –  Died 26 Apr 1920
  Largely self-taught Indian mathematician
  Other results still studied:
